THOUGHT: The previous sed edit corrupted `flipAnimation`: `final Spritesheet sprite = sprite;` is invalid and I still dereference `anim.getSpritesheet()` later. I need to fix this method to (1) obtain the spritesheet via `anim.getSpritesheet()`, (2) return `anim` early if it’s null, and (3) use the non-null local `sprite` for all subsequent calls (flip, width, height). Then I must rerun the build to ensure the original RETURN_NULLABLE error is gone, no new AnimationController errors exist, and the total NullAway error count is reduced by one.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/litiengine && sed -i '95,108c\  public static Animation flipAnimation(Animation anim, String newSpriteName) {
    final Spritesheet sprite = anim.getSpritesheet();
    if (sprite == null) {
      return anim;
    }
    final BufferedImage flippedImage = Imaging.flipSpritesHorizontally(sprite);
    Spritesheet flippedSpritesheet =
        Resources.spritesheets()
            .load(
                flippedImage,
                newSpriteName,
                sprite.getSpriteWidth(),
                sprite.getSpriteHeight());
    return new Animation(flippedSpritesheet, anim.isLooping(), anim.getKeyFrameDurations());
  }' src/de/gurkenlabs/litiengine/graphics/animation/AnimationController.java && ./gradlew compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && { grep -n "Animation.java" new_build_output.log || true; grep -n "AnimationController.java" new_build_output.log || true; tail -n 40 new_build_output.log | sed -n '/errors/p'; }
```

